  "originalQuery": "You are managing a large dataset on BigQuery that is accessed frequently during weekly business hours but seldom accessed outside of these hours. You want to minimize costs associated with querying this dataset while ensuring that query performance is maintained during high-access periods. What should you do?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Use BigQuery's automatic scaling feature to adjust resources in response to the query load.<br/>B. Convert the dataset to a partitioned table and set an expiration time for the partitions.<br/>C. Implement a BigQuery Reservation to allocate flex slots during high-access periods and release them afterward.<br/>D. Create a snapshot of the dataset and restore from it during high-access periods to expedite queries.",
  "domain": "Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud",
  "hasImage": false,
